  "answer": "To reduce the risk of excessive absorption losses in multi-layer optical systems, it has been proposed to deploy a Multi-Pass Deep Q-Network (MP-DQN) utilizing exponential reward shaping and Lagrangian regularisation (https://arxiv.org/abs/2010.05769). This operates via a mechanism that models the design as a parameterised Markov Decision Process (MDP) to jointly optimise discrete materials and continuous thickness parameters in a single optimisation loop (https://arxiv.org/abs/2010.05769). Specifically, the MP-DQN architecture uses separate networks: a *g* network proposes a thickness for each material, and an *f* network evaluates Q-values for each material-thickness pair and a terminate action (https://arxiv.org/abs/2010.05769)."
